01:08:47.310 --> 01:08:49.709
Subject is safety measures at railroad tracks.

01:08:49.790 --> 01:08:49.870
Ms.

01:08:49.979 --> 01:08:53.310
Hawkins, he'll come forward, he'll be followed by Andre Austin.

01:08:55.969 --> 01:09:01.087
Hi, my name is Jania Hawkins, and my address is 1538 Moontown Road,

01:09:01.167 --> 01:09:02.087
Brownsboro.

01:09:03.288 --> 01:09:05.309
Yes, um, good evening, everyone.

01:09:05.877 --> 01:09:10.889
Um, back in 2004, I actually lived on Salty Bottom Road with my family,

01:09:10.969 --> 01:09:16.167
my mom and my father, and he was hit by a train at that crossing,

01:09:16.249 --> 01:09:19.648
um, unprotected, unmarked crossing at Salty Bottom.

01:09:20.479 --> 01:09:25.008
After massive injuries that he incurred, he did survive,

01:09:25.127 --> 01:09:29.229
but survival is not the same as returning to the life he once had.

01:09:29.648 --> 01:09:32.087
After that day, his world became smaller,

01:09:32.207 --> 01:09:35.337
his strength, his independence, and the years that should have been spent

01:09:35.337 --> 01:09:39.249
spoiling his grandchildren were all limited by what happened in those few

01:09:39.249 --> 01:09:40.479
terrifying seconds.

01:09:40.809 --> 01:09:43.389
Our family has lived with that ever since.

01:09:44.219 --> 01:09:47.158
Then more recently, tragedy struck again.

01:09:47.337 --> 01:09:51.979
Last month, Keegan and McKinley Davis lost their lives at that same railroad

01:09:51.979 --> 01:09:53.499
tracks at Salty Bottom Road.

01:09:54.790 --> 01:09:56.470
Their family is here with us today.

01:09:56.709 --> 01:10:00.129
Um, his father and his daughter.

01:10:01.029 --> 01:10:04.009
Um, that actually was in the accident with them and survived.

01:10:04.319 --> 01:10:07.430
Um, lots of other supporters, if y'all would like to stand up just to show

01:10:07.430 --> 01:10:09.569
them who's here, would be great.

01:10:12.220 --> 01:10:15.580
The two lives that day was a 36-year-old father and an 8-year-old little

01:10:15.580 --> 01:10:19.370
girl gone in a moment that should have never been left so unprotected.

01:10:19.620 --> 01:10:22.819
Two families changed forever at a crossing that gave no warning,

01:10:22.970 --> 01:10:24.759
no barrier, and no second chance.

01:10:25.180 --> 01:10:27.819
These are not isolated stories, they're reminders.

01:10:27.899 --> 01:10:30.439
A train can't swerve, it can't stop quickly,

01:10:30.870 --> 01:10:33.720
and when a crossing has no lights, no gates,

01:10:34.140 --> 01:10:35.160
no protective.

01:10:36.129 --> 01:10:37.069
Barriers at all.

01:10:37.209 --> 01:10:41.250
The responsibility falls entirely on human judgment and the conditions are

01:10:41.250 --> 01:10:42.430
often hard to judge.

01:10:43.229 --> 01:10:45.299
This is why safety upgrades matter.

01:10:45.750 --> 01:10:48.669
Lights, bells, crossing arms are not luxuries.

01:10:48.790 --> 01:10:53.750
They're life-saving barriers between everyday travel and irreversible loss.

01:10:54.270 --> 01:10:58.430
Every crossing like Salty Bottom Road, a crossing that has more than 2100

01:10:58.430 --> 01:11:02.609
vehicles that cross it every single day, a crossing that's had multiple

01:11:02.609 --> 01:11:06.870
fatalities, a crossing that remains unprotected is a risk sitting in plain

01:11:06.870 --> 01:11:07.310
sight.

01:11:08.259 --> 01:11:12.620
City council members, I respectfully ask for your help along with all of

01:11:12.620 --> 01:11:16.180
these people and several that couldn't come because they couldn't get off

01:11:16.180 --> 01:11:16.799
work.

01:11:17.259 --> 01:11:21.060
In addressing the ongoing safety concerns at this railroad crossing at Salty

01:11:21.060 --> 01:11:25.620
Bottom, please work with Al Dot to make the necessary improvements before

01:11:25.620 --> 01:11:27.000
another tragedy occurs.

01:11:27.620 --> 01:11:31.899
If funding is the primary obstacle, I know there are some that have said

01:11:31.899 --> 01:11:35.700
they are willing to contribute toward the local matching funds that the

01:11:35.700 --> 01:11:38.759
county was previously unable or unwilling to provide.

01:11:39.879 --> 01:11:46.250
Our community continues to endure the devastating consequences of this dangerous

01:11:46.250 --> 01:11:47.009
crossing.

01:11:47.680 --> 01:11:48.620
Families are grieving.

01:11:48.799 --> 01:11:52.720
Lives have been forever changed, and the residents live with the fear that

01:11:52.720 --> 01:11:55.740
another preventable accident could happen anytime.

01:11:56.319 --> 01:11:59.879
We urge you to take action and help protect the citizens of our community

01:11:59.879 --> 01:12:01.500
from, from further loss.

01:12:02.270 --> 01:12:04.580
My father's life was altered in 2004.

01:12:05.160 --> 01:12:07.470
Keegan and McKinley Davis' lives were ended.

01:12:07.680 --> 01:12:09.419
We can't undo what's already happened, Ms.

01:12:10.000 --> 01:12:10.430
Hawkins.

01:12:10.520 --> 01:12:11.720
